Language English

Book Hall2 Ordered No Keep Looped

	// Hall2 can be explored from Hall1, the Foyer, or the Study

	Page ExploreHall2ViaHall1
		Triggered By @ExploreHall2ViaHall1
		
		Prolog """
			The hall seems to continue on a bit farther. An investigator in the
			same space as the Sight token can look down the hall.
		"""
		Button "Look down the hall"
		
		Remove SightHall2ViaHall1, SightHall2ViaFoyer, SightHall2ViaStudy
		Add TileHall2, TokenWallHall2!

		Text """
			With the dining room door so far from this end of the hall, you
			have to take a step forward to see what is there. Place the
			{c:TileHall2} tile and a wall as indicated. Discard all Sight and
			Explore tokens leading to this room.

			Move 1 space into the explored area.
		"""
		
		exploredHall2ViaHall1 = true
		Trigger @MoveAfterExplore
		Goto PlaceHall2
	End Page ExploreHall2ViaHall1
	
	Page ExploreHall2ViaFoyer
		Triggered By @ExploreHall2ViaFoyer
		
		Prolog """
			This door painted to blend. A casual visitor might not even notice
			it there.
		"""
		Button "Explore"
		
		Remove SightHall2ViaHall1, SightHall2ViaFoyer, SightHall2ViaStudy
		Add TileHall2, TokenWallHall2!

		Text """
			You realize this connects with the hallway you used to enter the
			gallery. Light from the foyer, even as dim as it, allows you to
			see into the room.
			
			Place the {c:TileHall2} tile and door as indicated. Remove all
			Sight and Explore tokens leading to this room.
		"""
		
		exploreHall2ViaVoyer = true
		Goto PlaceHall2
	End Page ExploreHall2ViaFoyer
	
	Page ExploreHall2ViaStudy
		Triggered By @ExploreHall2ViaStudy
		
		Prolog """
			This door is not labeled.
		"""
		Button "Explore"
		
		Remove SightHall2ViaHall1, SightHall2ViaFoyer, SightHall2ViaStudy
		Add TileHall2, TokenWallHall2!

		Text """
			Light from the study spills into the darkness. <<Oh,>> you say out
			loud, <<this leads back to the dining room.>> Place the
			{c:TileHall} and a door as indicated.
			
			Discard all Sight and Explore tokens leading to this room.
		"""

		exploredHall2ViaStudy = true
	End Page ExploreHall2ViaStudy
	
	Page PlaceHall2
		Text """
			A table has been knocked over, scattering its contents across the
			room. <i>That broken lamp on the floor would help navigate this 
			room,</i> you think to yourself. Place a Search token as indicated.
		"""
		
		If exploredHall2ViaFoyer Or exploredHall2ViaStudy Then Trigger @MoveAfterExplore
		exploredHall2 = true

		If exploredFoyer Or exploredStudy Then Exit
	End Page PlaceHall2
	
	
	Page PlaceExploreFoyerViaHall2
		Not Visible When exploredFoyer
		
		Add TokenExploreFoyerViaHall2!

		Text """
			Another door leads farther into the house. It has a small brass 
			plate that reads <<Foyer.>> Place an Explore token as indicated.
		"""	
		
		If exploredStudy Then Exit
	End Page PlaceExploreFoyerViaHall2

	Page PlaceHall2ExploreStudy
		Add TokenExploreStudyViaHall2!

		Text """
			Another door has a name plate that reads <<Study.>> Place an
			Explore token as indicated.
		"""
		
		Exit
	End Page PlaceHall2ExploreStudy
	
	Page SearchEvidence
		Triggered By @SearchHall2Evidence
		
		Prolog "The upended table has spilled its contents across the floor."
		
		Text """
			There is a dead plant and many scraps of paper tossed around. One
			of the scraps catches your eye:  it is spattered in dried blood.
			The note talks about preparations for a ritual and mentions
			something about a chapel and crypt that you don’t understand. The
			author of the note wants to stop the ritual and it is clear he will
			do what he can. The note is signed <<Henry Smythe.>>

			Gain the {c:QItemEvidenceHall2} Unique Item, then discard this
			Search token.
		"""

		Exit
	End Page SearchEvidence

End Book Hall2